The “already seen” list exists only during one run. A later run starts from the root again. If a White-move position was saved during an earlier run, the generator looks for it using the full position code, but the saved node uses a shortened position code. It therefore fails to find the node, tries to create the same move history again, and the database rejects it as a duplicate. The launcher catches the error and stops generation. Raising the depth cap and rerunning therefore does not extend an existing tree.
 ^d9NU4cxt

The depth cap of 3 
arrives from the launcher, 
not from the generator. 
Change the second argument in the launcher to use another depth cap. ^laCEud8B

