A1.24 · Print the temporary per-node checkpoint: elapsed time, nodes processed, branches aborted, white moves found, skipped, mainlines, traps, threats, and missing moves. ^yuCf13b8

The “already running” message reaches only the console. It is an error message, and A1.23 redirects only ordinary messages; A1.23 has not happened yet in any case. The later “Fatal Error” message also stays out of TreeGenLog.md. However, messages beginning “[ALERT - ERROR]” count as ordinary messages in the code, so they do reach the log file.
 ^uBuGE6yq

A1.25 · The generator first prints “Initializing BFS Tree Generator...”, then starts its timer and sets all its counters to zero. ^iaEffss2

The same position-code mismatch prevents the merge-and-skip checks from recognising saved nodes. A position reached by a different move order is saved as another node, and its Black reply is worked out again. If the exact same move history already exists from an earlier run, creating another node fails as a duplicate and stops the run, as the green note explains. ^dMPD94zG

The log is wiped before the lockfile is checked. If a second run is started while one is already running, it deletes the first run’s log so far and then quits. The first run itself keeps running and appends its later messages to the newly restarted log file.
 ^hkGYiwIb

